22.89766],[89.51838,22.89765],[89.5184,22.89874],[89.51869,22.89873],[89.5188,22.90469],[89.51851,22.90469],[89.51854,22.90605],[89.51824,22.90605],[89.51827,22.90767],[89.51798,22.90768],[89.51801,22.9093],[89.51684,22.90932]]]]},"river":{"type":"MultiLineString","coordinates":[]},"station":null,"checks":[{"id":7,"lat":22.85207,"lon":89.54895,"type":3,"agrees":false},{"id":10,"lat":22.83629,"lon":89.51944,"type":6,"agrees":true},{"id":14,"lat":22.83585,"lon":89.54719,"type":2,"agrees":true},{"id":16,"lat":22.83985,"lon":89.55106,"type":2,"agrees":true},{"id":17,"lat":22.83617,"lon":89.54457,"type":3,"agrees":false},{"id":21,"lat":22.83637,"lon":89.54866,"type":6,"agrees":false},{"id":26,"lat":22.84677,"lon":89.52489,"type":2,"agrees":true},{"id":28,"lat":22.84095,"lon":89.53297,"type":6,"agrees":false},{"id":31,"lat":22.83083,"lon":89.5395,"type":2,"agrees":false},{"id":35,"lat":22.8209,"lon":89.55071,"type":5,"agrees":true},{"id":38,"lat":22.84932,"lon":89.53487,"type":6,"agrees":true},{"id":40,"lat":22.83461,"lon":89.54015,"type":2,"agrees":true},{"id":43,"lat":22.8364,"lon":89.54691,"type":2,"agrees":false},{"id":44,"lat":22.8493,"lon":89.53634,"type":6,"agrees":true},{"id":49,"lat":22.82927,"lon":89.53567,"type":6,"agrees":false},{"id":53,"lat":22.85289,"lon":89.54868,"type":3,"agrees":false},{"id":59,"lat":22.84527,"lon":89.53392,"type":6,"agrees":true},{"id":72,"lat":22.84045,"lon":89.54727,"type":2,"agrees":true},{"id":76,"lat":22.8432,"lon":89.54499,"type":6,"agrees":true},{"id":80,"lat":22.82363,"lon":89.5493,"type":6,"agrees":true},{"id":90,"lat":22.84571,"lon":89.52341,"type":2,"agrees":true}],"texts":{"en":{"label":"Khulna City Corporation","area":"the city corporation","credit":"City corporation boundary from Practical Action Bangladesh, rivers from OpenStreetMap contributors","sources":"Maps: Landsat 8 and 9 (USGS), ESA WorldCover, the global Local Climate Zone map (Demuzere and others, 2022), city corporation boundary from Practical Action Bangladesh, rivers from OpenStreetMap contributors.","seasons":{"hot":{"name":"March to June","long":"March to June, the hot season","morning":"a clear morning in the hot season"}},"types":{"1":"Riverbank","2":"Green","3":"Bare ground","4":"Industrial","5":"Dense low rise","6":"Open low rise"},"layers":{"day":{"title":"Day surface temperature","note":"Ground, not air. Clear mornings around 10:30, March to June.","read":["How hot the ground and the roofs get in the sun on clear mornings. The darker the orange, the hotter.","Khulna is flat and humid, between rivers. By day roofs, yards and bare ground heat up most, and wet fields, water and trees stay coolest. The maps still show the ground, not the air people breathe, so they are not heat risk maps."],"sure":["About 2 °C over uniform ground, more over mixed roofs and streets. The real detail is about 100 m.","Where fewer than 10 clear images exist, cloud may be left in the colour. Mostly clear mornings are rare in March to June, about three a year, and the clearest are probably drier than most. The clear winter mornings, November to February, are far more common (159 almost cloud free ones). Their pattern agrees closely with the hot season one, with the same places warm and cool, and the differences are about 1.7 times larger in the hot season. So the pattern on this map holds beyond the few mornings it rests on."],"box":"This is the ground and the roofs. On a sunny morning a roof or bare ground can be 10 to 20 °C hotter than the air above it. It is not a heat risk map.","details":[["Shows","How hot the ground and the roofs get in the sun."],["Unit","Degrees Celsius at the surface."],["Time","Clear mornings around 10:30."],["Period","March to June, 2014 to 2026, Landsat 8 and 9."],["Accuracy","About 2 °C over uniform ground, more over mixed roofs and streets. The real detail is about 100 m."],["Clear images","45 per point on average, from 0 to 62."]]},"relative":{"title":"Relative to typical settled ground","note":"Ground, not air. Clear mornings around 10:30, March to June.","read":["Each place is compared with typical settled ground across the city corporation. Red runs warmer than a typical neighbourhood, blue runs cooler, white is about the same."],"sure":["The satellite cannot reliably tell apart differences under about 1 °C.","Colours fade where fewer than 10 clear images exist, since the colour says less there. The values are unchanged."],"box":"This is the ground and the roofs. On a sunny morning a roof or bare ground can be 10 to 20 °C hotter than the air above it. It is not a heat risk map.","details":[["Shows","All ground. Zero is the typical settled surface across the city corporation, so the map shows which places run hotter or cooler than typical settled ground."],["Unit","Degrees Celsius warmer (red) or cooler (blue)."],["Zero","39 °C."],["Time","Clear mornings around 10:30."],["Period","March to June, 2014 to 2026, Landsat 8 and 9."],["Clear images","45 per point on average, from 0 to 62."]]},"type1":{"title":"Riverbank","note":"1% of the city corporation. Each point stands for about 100 m around it.","read":["The kind of place at each point, from global land cover and urban climate maps: riverbank within 150 m of the Rupsha and the Bhairab, green (trees, grass, crops), bare ground, and three kinds of settled ground (industrial, dense low rise, open low rise).","Each point stands for about 100 m around it, since a sensor speaks for its surroundings."],"sure":["We compared 15 random points of this type against high resolution satellite imagery. The type was right at 3 of them.","The check points on the map show where we looked."],"box":"","details":[["Share","1% of the city corporation."],["Sources","ESA WorldCover and the global Local Climate Zone map (Demuzere and others, 2022)."]]},"type2":{"title":"Green","note":"44% of the city corporation. Each point stands for about 100 m around it.","read":["The kind of place at each point, from global land cover and urban climate maps: riverbank within 150 m of the Rupsha and the Bhairab, green (trees, grass, crops), bare ground, and three kinds of settled ground (industrial, dense low rise, open low rise).","Each point stands for about 100 m around it, since a sensor speaks for its surroundings."],"sure":["We compared 15 random points of this type against high resolution satellite imagery. The type was right at 10 of them.","The check points on the map show where we looked."],"box":"","details":[["Share","44% of the city corporation."],["Sources","ESA WorldCover and the global Local Climate Zone map (Demuzere and others, 2022)."]]},"type3":{"title":"Bare ground","note":"1% of the city corporation. Each point stands for about 100 m around it.","read":["The kind of place at each point, from global land cover and urban climate maps: riverbank within 150 m of the Rupsha and the Bhairab, green (trees, grass, crops), bare ground, and three kinds of settled ground (industrial, dense low rise, open low rise).","Each point stands for about 100 m around it, since a sensor speaks for its surroundings."],"sure":["We compared 15 random points of this type against high resolution satellite imagery. The type was right at 1 of them.","The check points on the map show where we looked."],"box":"","details":[["Share","1% of the city corporation."],["Sources","ESA WorldCover and the global Local Climate Zone map (Demuzere and others, 2022)."]]},"type4":{"title":"Industrial","note":"2% of the city corporation. Each point stands for about 100 m around it.","read":["The kind of place at each point, from global land cover and urban climate maps: riverbank within 150 m of the Rupsha and the Bhairab, green (trees, grass, crops), bare ground, and three kinds of settled ground (industrial, dense low rise, open low rise).","Each point stands for about 100 m around it, since a sensor speaks for its surroundings."],"sure":["We compared 15 random points of this type against high resolution satellite imagery. The type was right at 6 of them.","The check points on the map show where we looked."],"box":"","details":[["Share","2% of the city corporation."],["Sources","ESA WorldCover and the global Local Climate Zone map (Demuzere and others, 2022)."]]},"type5":{"title":"Dense low rise","note":"5% of the city corporation. Each point stands for about 100 m around it.","read":["The kind of place at each point, from global land cover and urban climate maps: riverbank within 150 m of the Rupsha and the Bhairab, green (trees, grass, crops), bare ground, and three kinds of settled ground (industrial, dense low rise, open low rise).","Each point stands for about 100 m around it, since a sensor speaks for its surroundings."],"sure":["We compared 15 random points of this type against high resolution satellite imagery. The type was right at 15 of them.","The check points on the map show where we looked."],"box":"","details":[["Share","5% of the city corporation."],["Sources","ESA WorldCover and the global Local Climate Zone map (Demuzere and others, 2022)."]]},"type6":{"title":"Open low rise","note":"47% of the city corporation. Each point stands for about 100 m around it.","read":["The kind of place at each point, from global land cover and urban climate maps: riverbank within 150 m of the Rupsha and the Bhairab, green (trees, grass, crops), bare ground, and three kinds of settled ground (industrial, dense low rise, open low rise).","Each point stands for about 100 m around it, since a sensor speaks for its surroundings."],"sure":["We compared 15 random points of this type against high resolution satellite imagery. The type was right at 11 of them.","The check points on the map show where we looked."],"box":"","details":[["Share","47% of the city corporation."],["Sources","ESA WorldCover and the global Local Climate Zone map (Demuzere and others, 2022)."]]}},"seen":{"1":"Green","2":"Dense low rise","5":"Green","6":"Green","7":"Industrial","9":"Open low rise","13":"Industrial","17":"Green","19":"R